    "result_text": "A steward can now move a DRAFT, OPEN or PENDING claim to another person on the sheet. `bin/e2e` passes.\n\n**How it behaves**\n- Each claim row has a \"Move to\u2026\" person picker (`claim-reassign-to`) and a Move button (`claim-reassign`). The picker lists everyone on the sheet except the claim's current person.\n- The claim keeps its number, date and status. Only its person changes, and all totals follow because the screen works them out from each claim's person.\n- After a successful move, `CLAIM_REASSIGNED` is written in the same format as the other claim lines (naming the new person), ending `from=<old name> to=<new name>`.\n- A refused move shows `claim-error` on the claim and writes nothing.\n\n**What gets refused.** The request only said a settled or voided claim can't move. The other refusals below are my own choices, made to match the rules other actions already follow:\n- the user isn't a steward\n- the claim is SETTLED or VOID\n- no person is chosen, or it's the claim's own person\n- the claim is dated inside a closed period\n- the claim is dated after the new person retired\n- the claim is a correction. A correction has to point to a settled claim of the same person, so moving it would break that link.\n\n**Where the changes are**\n- **Server:** a new `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/claims/{claimId}/reassign` route (`reassign.POST.yml`), with new classes `ValidateReassignment`, `ReassignClaim`, `AuditClaimReassigned`, `ReassignRequest` and `Reassignment`. `Claim` also gained a `setPersonId` setter. No database migration was needed.\n- **Front end:** `canReassign` and `reassignClaim` in `features/claims/claims.ts`, and the picker, button and screen-side checks in `claims.slot.tsx`.",
